WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:03.408
(dramatic music)

00:00:03.408 --> 00:00:06.440
(dog panting)
(suspenseful music)

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.810
- AirTag not reachable.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.100
Move around to connect.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:09.933
Wasabi.

00:00:11.503 --> 00:00:13.002
To my left.

00:00:13.002 --> 00:00:15.170
(dog sniffing)

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.640
Oh wait.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.830
(dramatic music)

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.100
Allow me to explain.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.010
This is my fanny pack

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.350
and attached to it is an Apple AirTag,

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.640
a new $29 gadget that you
attach to items you often lose.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.800
So you could find them using
your iPhone's Find My app.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.690
This is Wasabi, a
professional detection dog

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.360
that can sniff out the
most hidden of items.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.850
And well, I think you
can tell where I went

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.980
with this whole thing.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.070
I put this AirTag and other
competing lost item trackers,

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.920
like the Tile Pro and Samsung SmartTag

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.650
up against Wasabi's nose

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.200
in a series of indoor and
outdoor hiding challenges

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.700
because well, yeah, my
dog only moves for bacon.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.854
Up.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:55.687
(hands clapping)

00:00:55.687 --> 00:00:56.520
Do anything.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.880
And since many have been
asking if AirTags could be used

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:00.660
as a pet tracker, there you go,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.780
we put one Wasabi for
a separate challenge.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.770
Of course, Alisa, Wasabi's owner

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.060
and professional narcotic
K9 handler with 3DK9

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.770
was along for the whole ride,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.320
ensuring Wasabi was happy,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.053
healthy and hydrated.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.900
All right, here we go.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.530
Challenge one, fanny
pack lost in the house.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.660
AirTags and other lost item trackers

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.210
use lower-powered Bluetooth

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.820
to stay constantly connected

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.773
up to several hundred feet away.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.230
Wasabi's sniff range?

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.860
It depends on a lot of factors

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.350
but about five feet in every direction.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.870
For this challenge, we
had him sniff out drugs,

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.790
fake drugs, more specifically,

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.570
a substance that smells like heroin.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.790
Yeah, it definitely smells.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.220
But is absolutely not heroin.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.800
It's used in K9 training.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:49.940
Instead of using my nose,

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.850
I used my ears for this challenge.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.660
When you're in range of an AirTag,

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.000
you can press on this button

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.150
in the Find My app to sound an alarm

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.870
on the tracker itself.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.710
So I had my producer Kenny
here hide the fanny pack

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.970
someplace inside my townhouse.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.193
- And I'm gonna wrap it.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.678
You can't hear the dangles.

00:02:07.678 --> 00:02:10.428
(dramatic music)

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.940
- [Joanna] Of course,
Wasabi found the fanny pack

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.220
in one minute and 20 seconds.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.449
- Yes.
- Yo.

00:02:23.449 --> 00:02:24.282
Hey, yeah.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.160
- Me and the AirTags?

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.050
Okay, not so quick.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.570
I knew it wasn't on the basement floor

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.530
because I don't hear anything in here.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:34.780
When I hit the second floor,

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:38.570
Apple's precision finding
feature came in super handy.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.540
It says connected but the signal's weak,

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.410
so it's not in this area
but I hear the sound.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.050
Tap Find Nearby in the app

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.450
and it uses ultra-wideband technology,

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.310
which is more precise than Bluetooth

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.520
in very close distances.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.450
If you're within a couple
of feet of the item

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.710
and you have an iPhone
with ultra-wideband,

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:56.970
the iPhone 11 and up,

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.180
it can guide you to the item

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.290
with on-screen directions.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.370
Fanny pack may be on a
different level than you

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.040
unless it thinks it's
upstairs in this area.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.493
And so what?

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.073
Bathroom?

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.223
Nearby here.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.373
Whoa, I found it.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.610
Got it.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.520
I also tested the Samsung and
the Tile in the same location.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.210
The Samsung and the Tile's alarms

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.180
were louder and I could hear them clearer

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.690
from the second floor.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.230
But they lack ultra-wideband,

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.500
so no detailed on-screen instructions

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.680
about the direction of the object.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:35.933
The winner?

00:03:35.933 --> 00:03:36.766
(Wasabi barking)

00:03:36.766 --> 00:03:37.720
Obviously.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.220
Challenge two.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.679
Funny pack lost outside.

00:03:41.679 --> 00:03:44.346
(playful music)

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.430
- The planter and you can't
see it from the street.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.640
- All the trackers' apps show the location

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.520
of where your phone

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.930
and the tracker were last connected.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.580
In this case, where I
had the fanny pack last,

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.110
standing on this street corner.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:02.350
But Apple's Find My
network goes a bit further.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.970
Anyone's iPhone in the real world

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.450
can report the location of an AirTag.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.560
Think of it as an invisible network.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.860
Whenever an iPhone passes the AirTag,

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.430
it anonymously and unknowingly picks up

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.000
that Bluetooth signal

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.490
and the location of where it picked it up.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.810
The owner of the AirTag

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.930
can then see the location
in the Find My app.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.040
Tile and Samsung have similar networks

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.720
but in this case, it's likely that no one

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.460
with a participating Samsung phone

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.840
or the Tile app on their phone walked by

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.900
but a billion active iPhones in the world

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.130
is a big AirTag selling point.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.670
The Find My app says

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.370
that it is on the corner
of Newark over there.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.960
Tile has no idea where it is.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.350
But once that Find My
app led us into that 10

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:45.100
to 15-foot range,

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.228
Wasabi took off.

00:04:47.228 --> 00:04:49.630
(beep)

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.020
All right, so if I'm standing over here,

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.230
it's on the corner over here.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.063
No.

00:04:57.581 --> 00:04:59.322
Arg, damn you.

00:04:59.322 --> 00:05:00.183
- Yes.

00:05:00.183 --> 00:05:01.520
- You wouldn't have known
it over here, Wasabi

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:03.000
if it wasn't for me.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.253
Winner, AirTags and Wasabi.

00:05:07.021 --> 00:05:08.160
(dramatic music)

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.560
Challenge three.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.710
Dog lost.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.880
All right, go anywhere
within 10-mile radius,

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.930
turn your phone on airplane mode

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:17.880
and wait there.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:18.960
Before sending them off,

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.160
I equipped Wasabi with two trackers,

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.770
an AirTag and the Whistle Go Explore,

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.600
a real pet tracker.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.890
With the Whistle, I had a live GPS view

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.300
of where they were headed.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.820
The device connects to
AT&amp;T's cellular network,

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:34.760
which is why in addition
to the $150 device,

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.660
you have to pay a subscription fee.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:41.490
Then it says that Wasabi is
currently on Freedom Way.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.370
You zoom out.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.353
That seems to be Liberty State Park.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.730
- [GPS] Turn left onto Freedom Way.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:51.843
- With the AirTag,

00:05:51.843 --> 00:05:54.790
it was similar to the lost
fanny pack on the street.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.040
I had to wait until
someone with an iPhone came

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.280
into contact with the AirTag at the park

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.593
to see the location.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.050
Wasabi.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.133
Ah, I see Wasabi over there.

00:06:08.748 --> 00:06:11.210
As you so impressed that I found you.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:12.043
The winner?

00:06:12.043 --> 00:06:14.910
The Whistle, through the
AirTags held their own,

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:17.280
plus the Whistle drops battery quick.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.090
The AirTags have replaceable batteries

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.300
that are said to last up to a year.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.830
So what did we learn here today?

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.130
Well, that everyone should get a Wasabi.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:27.130
But really, AirTags are very good.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.360
The lost mode feature needs improvement,

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.080
it sucks that you have to buy an accessory

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.630
to make sure you don't
lose the actual AirTag

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.860
and despite Apple's
anti-stalking features,

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:37.690
I have fears about these
being used secretly

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:38.880
to track people.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.376
But if you often lose things,

00:06:40.376 --> 00:06:44.233
the only other real option
is to well, not lose them.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.500
Guys, I've gotta get a real dog.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.263
I love you, Browser, I love you.

